cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Kannada Legacy Encodings specification, tables or benchmark, please cite them as below."
title: "Kannada Legacy Encodings: an open specification and conformance suite for legacy Kannada font text"
abstract: "An open specification, glyph tables and conformance tests for converting text typed in the legacy Kannada font layouts Nudi, Baraha ANSI, Akruti, Shree-Lipi, Nudi B-Akshara and Kan-Eng to Unicode, with a reference reader and a benchmark of 5,098 lines from 275 Karnataka government PDFs."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Subrahmanya
    given-names: Prasad
    website: "https://prasad.tech"
repository-code: "https://github.com/openkannada/legacy-encodings"
url: "https://openkannada.org/nudi-to-unicode/"
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
  - CC-BY-4.0
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - kannada
  - unicode
  - legacy fonts
  - nudi
  - baraha
  - conformance testing
